THE FINDING
  aggregate change   -37495
  established?       false
  leading cell       Northeast -> Northeast-2 -> Outdoor
  its change         -16835
  established?       true

  So ONE cell is real and the aggregate is not. That is not a corner
  case -- it is what the data said, and the decision has to survive it.

THE DECISION: spend 15000 to recover 60% of the loss?

  sized off the aggregate decline:
    loss taken as    -37495
    expected benefit 22497
    cost             -15000
    expected value   7497
    -> ACT
  sized off the cell that cleared:
    loss taken as    -16835
    expected benefit 10101
    cost             -15000
    expected value   -4899
    -> DO NOT ACT

  THE SAME INTERVENTION, THE SAME DATA, OPPOSITE ANSWERS. The only
  difference is which number was taken as the loss -- and the Finding
  already said the aggregate was not established.

AUTHORITY: this process may spend up to 5000 unattended.

  do nothing                 EV 0         within authority
  send a regional manager    EV 1000      within authority
  restock and promote        EV 7497      needs approval

  best option overall:            restock and promote (EV 7497)
  best option within authority:   send a regional manager (EV 1000)

  A decision layer that quietly returned the second one would be
  hiding the only choice a human actually needs to make. The
  recommendation is the FIRST; authority is a separate field, and it
  is enforced later, at the action (design R6).
